          "type": "multipleCorrect",
          "level": 1,
          "question": {
            "text": "Among the following, the correct statement(s) about polymers is(are)",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "aE4es",
              "text": "The polymerization of chloroprene gives natural rubber.",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "mMtXP",
              "text": "Teflon is prepared from tetrafluoroethene by heating it with persulphate catalyst at high pressures.",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "up3Th",
              "text": "PVC are thermoplastic polymers.",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5v7ta",
              "text": "Ethene at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>570</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;temperature and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2000</mn></math> atm pressure in the presence of a peroxide initiator yields high density polythene.",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<p>(A) Polymerization of chloroprene gives synthetic rubber</p><p>(B) Teflon is manufactured by heating tetrafluoroethene with a free radical or persulphate catalyst at hight pressure.</p><p>(C) Polyvinyl chloride (PVC) is a thermoplastic polymer and used in making hand bags, vinyl flooring and water pipes.</p><p>(D) Ethene at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>570</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> temperature and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math> pressure in the presence of a peroxide initiator yields low density polythene.</p>",
            "image": null
          },
